program	conformance/U30_generic_instantiation_unsafe_signature.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	`idn` is not declared `unsafe`, but this instantiation's signature names a value of unsafe type (`UnsafePointer<Int8>`)
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: `idn` is not declared `unsafe`, but this instantiation's signature names a value of unsafe type (`UnsafePointer<Int8>`)"
log	"  --> examples/conformance/U30_generic_instantiation_unsafe_signature.saw:25:13"
log	"     |"
log	" 25 |     let p = idn(make_ptr())"
log	"     |             ^"
log	"   hint: declare the generic `unsafe` — calling an unsafe function from safe code needs no ceremony, so the marker costs its other instantiations nothing and buys every reader a signature that tells the truth. Or keep the unsafe type out of the type argument"
log	""
log	"1 error(s) generated"
